<title>SOUTH KOREA: Ssangyong files suit vs Tokyo client.</title>
<headline>Ssangyong files suit vs Tokyo client.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Ssangyong Investment and Securities Co said on Tuesday it has filed a civil lawsuit in Tokyo against a client who failed to pay 1.61 billion yen for share purchases.</p>
<p>The Ssangyong Group unit said in a statement the client requested its Tokyo branch to buy 3.72 billion yen worth of stocks but failed to pay 1.61 billion yen, including 4.37 million yen in commissions.</p>
<p>It gave no further details. ($1 = 122 yen)</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5646</p>
